extends Node

"""

Episodes 1–2: Setup & Inciting Incident
Ep 1: Introduce main characters, their personal struggles, and why they re not ready for love. They meet—maybe clash or misunderstand each other.

Ep 2: They’re forced into a situation that keeps them around each other (e.g., work, family, fake dating, stranded, etc.). A spark forms.

Episodes 3–4: Bonding & Emotional Growth
Ep 3: Start to see layers beyond first impressions. Maybe they help each other in a moment of vulnerability.

Ep 4: Subplots build their connection (e.g., solving a problem together, flashbacks, shared interests). Chemistry builds but is still unspoken.

Episodes 5–6: Midpoint Romance & Inner Conflict
Ep 5: A breakthrough or a near-kiss moment. They connect deeply—but something holds them back (trauma, external obligations, pride).

Ep 6: Things go too well—then an external force (ex-partner, job change, a secret revealed) disrupts the momentum.

Episodes 7–8: Breakup or Separation
Ep 7: Conflict explodes—harsh words, betrayal, or fear of commitment. They go separate ways or avoid each other.

Ep 8: Characters reflect, grow, and confront their own flaws. Realization: they need each other not out of dependency, but true love.

Episodes 9–10: Climax & Resolution
Ep 9: One or both take a leap—grand gesture, confession, or sacrifice. Tension and emotion peak.

Ep 10: Full resolution—reunion or bittersweet closure. Side plots are wrapped. The romance feels earned and satisfying.




"""
